From d71a18be2780731dd323a49474ca58e46364908a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pepopepopepo <311073437+pepopepopepo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 00:04:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: build the patched clangd at the installed LLVM's version
 (make clangd)

packaging/clangd-index-nav/PKGBUILD pinned pkgver=23.1.1 while the
distribution ships llvm-libs 23.1.3, so on a current system the package
neither built (makedepends llvm=23.1.1) nor installed, and every LLVM
release meant editing pkgver and the checksums by hand. The exact
depends on llvm-libs and clang stay (D-027: the binary links the system
libLLVM and reads the system clangd's shards); what changes is who
writes the version. scripts/build-clangd.sh (new) writes pkgver from
`llvm-config --version` when it differs, refreshes the checksums with
updpkgsums (pacman-contrib), checks that llvm-libs matches, and runs
makepkg with the flags given; `make clangd MAKEPKG_FLAGS=-si` is the
README's install step now. The PKGBUILD is committed at 23.1.3, the
version the script wrote on a current system; pkgrel stays 9 (it counts
the patch series, not the LLVM release).

Checked: the 13 patches apply unchanged on 23.1.3 (`makepkg --nobuild`
through the target, 70 files patched, no offset, no fuzz), and a full
`makepkg` on 23.1.3 built clangd in 7.5 minutes on 32 threads with the
PKGBUILD's check() passing; `make check` ok.

Reasoning:
What was wrong: a hand-maintained pkgver that falls behind the rolling
  release; the first symptom on an upgraded machine is "cannot be
  installed", not "rebuild".
Evidence: pacman -Q llvm-libs 23.1.3-2 against pkgver=23.1.1; the
  scratch build at 23.1.3 (review B-1, R5).
Ruled out: loosening depends to >= (the shard format and libLLVM
  soname change per release; D-027's reason holds); reading pacman's
  version inside the PKGBUILD (makepkg forbids it; a wrapper is the
  Arch way, as updpkgsums is).
Tier: 2

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
